    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup heavily incentivized by stolen base upside and favorable platoon dynamics. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (69.33) and **Caleb Durbin** (68.14) headline our start list, both benefiting significantly from facing pitchers with slow deliveries that maximize their high-end speed profiles. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** specifically benefits from an elite platoon edge (+14%) against Cade Cavalli, while **Caleb Durbin** leverages a strong SP skill matchup against Max Scherzer to secure his status as an anchor for the team\u2019s efficiency today. Despite the 5.10 xERA of the opposing starter, we are banking on these two to ignite the Roto categories through their aggressiveness on the basepaths.\n\nElsewhere, **Chase Meidroth** (66.48) provides high-floor production leading off against A.J. Abbott; his projected 19% SP skill advantage and the +10% order bonus solidify his status as a lock. We are keeping a close eye on **Trea Turner** (59.73), whose score is slightly tempered by a \"Wind In\" factor (-5%) at the park, though his inherent speed profile and position in the two-hole against Taj Bradley keep him firmly in the \"Strong\" start tier. Conversely, **Kazuma Okamoto** (48.46) represents our most marginal play today, as a 17% penalty against the SP skill of Payton Tolle nearly relegated him to the pine.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Pedro Ramirez** (39.24), who missed the cut primarily due to his lower-order placement. While his switch-hitting ability and park factors were favorable, the optimizer prioritized the higher projected base efficiency of **Dillon Dingler** (55.79), whose dynamic platoon advantage against a lefty more than offsets the SP skill risk. Be advised that nearly our entire outfield and utility corps are subject to \"Lineup Pending\" designations; while we have assumed positions for **Gary Sanchez**, **Christian Yelich**, and **Kyle Schwarber**, any significant deviation in the final cards\u2014particularly if any of our speed-threats are bumped out of the top two spots\u2014could force a re-evaluation of our daily total.",
